Z||000000||Loki||06-17-2001||11:36 PM||||Im looking at redoing my headliner (3rd break light and sunroof)  How much of an over lap to tuck into sunroof trim?<BR><P>------------------<BR>Loki<BR>ICQ# 16477998||||reg||1
Z||000001||AusFiero||06-17-2001||11:46 PM||||From experiences I have had Loki just leave heaps more than you need, once glued you can trim any excess off when you see where the edge will be hidden. Can always trim, can never add.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/fiero5.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A><BR>Need a Subwoofer Console or Speaker Door Pods?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||06-18-2001||05:03 AM||||If anyone's familiar with leather, would they be kind enough to go to <A HREF="http://www.justleather.com" TARGET=_blank>www.justleather.com</A>  and tell me what grade, etc of their leather is thin enough to use on my headliner?  I'm planning on buying some leather from them to cover: lower door panels, sub box, either firewall or future amp rack, and sunvisors.  Covering the headliner would certainly add to the look.  (Of course, Mr. Mikes seat covers will be in the future, too.)<P>MM||||reg||1
Z||000003||tgowens||06-18-2001||05:29 AM||||Loki, leave about four to five inches in the sunroof area (tuck it in, attach the bead, and trim excess if necessary) and on the front and rear (which you tuck over and glue) - everything else (sides, brake light, dome light, sunroof latch) can be trimmed out.........<P>Also, I use a credit card (or similar material) to tuck the material into the channel......it has rounded edges and corners and will not tear the material.....<P>Hope this helps.....||||reg||1
Z||000004||Loki||06-18-2001||07:51 AM||||Thanx for the info   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>Loki<BR>ICQ# 16477998||||reg||1
